  {
   "line": 4,
   "text": "Lesson three's wheel. A tone is a turning dot, and a sample is its left-right shadow. Twice the samples, half the turn. One thousand hertz turns twenty-two and a half degrees. Seven thousand turns one hundred fifty-seven and a half, under half a turn, so here it's a real tone.",
