  {
   "line": 9,
   "text": "Going down, the bridge keeps every other sample. That's downsampling. The hiss of an S, at six thousand hertz, lands on your line as a two thousand hertz squeal, an alias across the same mirror. So the low-pass filter goes first, gain one, while six thousand is still six thousand.",
